{"term":"back up","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0cb9523f8cdd9fe23d","definition":"To move backwards, especially for a vehicle to do so.","example":"That beeping sound indicates that the truck is backing up.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, intransitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f5e9b5117ee2f907c7","definition":"To move a vehicle backwards.","example":"Back up the car a little, you're blocking the driveway.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["reverse"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f883553a89f2980bda","definition":"To undo one's actions.","example":"I couldn't see how to finish the project, so I backed up and tried it another way.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["back out"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, intransitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:44f73f2b2704f0f19b","definition":"To reconsider one's thoughts.","example":"This isn't working. Let's back up and think about it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, intransitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b48ee72bb95550e6f2","definition":"To copy (data) so that it can be restored if the main copy is lost.","example":"Back up your documents folder before applying the update.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:394fc2d54e6d57d6b4","definition":"To provide support or the promise of support to.","example":"You should be careful. This guy is backed up by the local gang.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["back","support"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ae482e3b0d8f9f4353","definition":"For the non-striker to take a few steps down the pitch, in preparation to taking a run, just as the bowler bowls the ball.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, intransitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c4d179b69822a3949a","definition":"For a fielder to position himself behind the wicket (relative to a team-mate who is throwing the ball at the wicket) so as to stop the ball, and prevent overthrows.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, intransitive","wordFamily":["backupable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionar